ed the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows    Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells    Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells    Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 27   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11 43 18AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID