ed and verified the test s accuracy and precision Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  156  to chromosome 17 signals  137  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE  2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results   Lymphoma Workup RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STUDIES ON PARAFFIN SECTIONS  Studies performed at MGH  The lymph node architecture is effaced by a proliferation of small lymphocytes  Scattered pale staining areas are seen containing larger cells  prolymphocytes  paraimmunoblasts   consistent with proliferation centers  With B lineage antibodies  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and PAX 5  there is staining of most cells in a diffuse pattern  The B cells are positive for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and are negative for cyclin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Residual reactive follicles at the periphery of the lymph node are bcl6   With T lineage antibody  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of many small cells scattered within the tissue  A stain for Ki67 shows an appropriately high level of staining in reactive follicles  The lymphoma cells show a very low proliferation index   5    with slightly increased staining within proliferation centers  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results confirm the diagnosis of SMALL LYMPHOCYTIC LYMPHOMA  CONSISTEN